.TH WSL-TOOLKIT 1 "" "wsl-toolkit 3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wsl-toolkit \- run isolated Linux container jobs from Windows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
wsl-toolkit 3.0.0

  doctor      report the host and the tools that can run
  base        manage the WSL distribution that this tool owns
  images      list, check, or pull catalog images
  run         run one command in one container
  matrix      run one command across a set of images
  resources   report resources that this tool owns
  gc          report or remove resources that this tool owns
  logs        read the complete output from one job
  inspect     inspect one job and its recorded host state
  helper      manage the optional local WSL helper
  config      report, validate, or write the configuration
  distro      create, use, observe and remove throwaway WSL distributions built from an image or a rootfs
  hostaddress print the address a WSL distribution reaches this host at
  bsd         run a command in a FreeBSD guest on this host's own hypervisor
  ready       test whether this host can run an isolated Linux job
  selfupdate  verify and install a published release
  artifacts   retrieve an artifact copy that a failed transfer retained
  examples    print the canonical command examples
  man         open or print the manual generated from the registered CLI
  version     print the product version

Global: --instance N  one isolated instance: distribution wsl-toolkit-N and
                      its own state. `auto` picks the lowest free one.
                      Also WSL_TOOLKIT_INSTANCE.
        --home DIR    the state directory (also WSL_TOOLKIT_HOME)
        --config F    a configuration file, ahead of every search step
        --quiet       progress off. Answers still go to stdout

Every command takes --json where an answer has structure.
Progress goes to stderr; stdout carries the answer alone.
.fi
