raw, human, ci, forensic or wall. Empty forwards the command's streams unchanged. Flags passed beside a profile win over it
.TP
\fB--max-line-bytes\fR
cut a line after this many bytes, at a character boundary, and say how many went. 0 never cuts
.TP
\fB--prefix-only\fR
write the timestamp prefix and not the line itself
.TP
\fB--redact\fR
a regular expression whose matches become *** before any sink sees a line. Repeatable; a comma list is accepted, and [,] is a literal comma
.TP
\fB--run\fR
render only this run of an appended log, counting from 1. 0 renders every run
.TP
\fB--timestamp-column\fR
a timestamp column: rel, delta, wall, iso or epoch. Repeatable; a comma list is accepted
.TP
\fB--timestamp-format\fR
a strftime format for the rel and wall columns: %Y %m %d %H %M %S %z %Z %3f %6f %9f %%
.TP
\fB--timestamp-mode\fR
one timestamp column: rel, delta, wall, iso or epoch
.TP
\fB--timestamp-separator\fR
the text between the timestamp columns and the tag. Default:  .
.TP
.B wsl-toolkit distro compare
.TP
\fB--after\fR
the later wsl-toolkit-event/1 file
.TP
\fB--after-run\fR
the run of --after to compare, counting from 1. 0 is its last run
.TP
\fB--before\fR
the earlier wsl-toolkit-event/1 file
.TP
\fB--before-run\fR
the run of --before to compare, counting from 1. 0 is its last run
.TP
\fB--json\fR
write the structured comparison
.SS hostaddress
print the address a WSL distribution reaches this host at
.TP
.B wsl-toolkit hostaddress
.TP
\fB--json\fR
write a structured answer
.SS bsd
run a command in a FreeBSD guest on this host's own hypervisor
.TP
.B wsl-toolkit bsd status
.TP
\fB--json\fR
write a structured answer
.TP
.B wsl-toolkit bsd fetch
.TP
\fB--force\fR
fetch again even when a verified image is already here
.TP
\fB--json\fR
write a structured answer
.TP
.B wsl-toolkit bsd run
.TP
\fB--c\fR
the command to run at a root shell in the guest
.TP
\fB--cpus\fR
guest processor count. Default: 1.
.TP
\fB--disk\fR
guest disk in GiB. The image grows to it and never shrinks, and the root filesystem follows in the guest. Default: 12.
.TP
\fB--json\fR
write a structured answer
.TP
\fB--memory\fR
guest memory in MiB. Default: 2048.
.TP
\fB--network\fR
give the guest outbound user-mode networking. Nothing is forwarded inward
.TP
\fB--no-console\fR
do not mirror the guest console while it boots
.TP
\fB--script\fR
a file whose contents run at a root shell in the guest
.TP
\fB--timeout\fR
the whole session, the boot included. Default: 15m0s.
.SS ready
test whether this host can run an isolated Linux job
.TP
.B wsl-toolkit ready
.TP
\fB--ensure\fR
build or repair the base if it is not usable
.TP
\fB--json\fR
write a structured answer
.TP
\fB--no-update\fR
do not ask whether a newer release exists
.TP
\fB--smoke\fR
run one tiny container proving the whole path
.SS selfupdate
verify and install a published release
.TP
.B wsl-toolkit selfupdate
.TP
\fB--check\fR
report whether a newer release exists and change nothing
.TP
\fB--json\fR
write a structured answer
.TP
\fB--tag\fR
a specific release tag, so a caller can move down as well as up
.SS artifacts
retrieve an artifact copy that a failed transfer retained
.TP
.B wsl-toolkit artifacts retry
.TP
\fB--json\fR
write a structured answer
.TP
\fB--to\fR
the directory to write the retained copy into
.SS examples
print the canonical command examples
.TP
.B wsl-toolkit examples
.TP
\fB--json\fR
write a structured answer
.SS man
open or print the manual generated from the registered CLI
.TP
.B wsl-toolkit man
.TP
\fB--no-pager\fR
write the complete readable manual to stdout
.TP
\fB--output\fR
write the generated roff man page to this file
.SS version
print the product version
.TP
.B wsl-toolkit version
.TP
\fB--json\fR
write a structured answer
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
is this machine ready
.nf
wsl-toolkit ready --smoke
.fi
.TP
one persistent command in one container
.nf
wsl-toolkit run --image alpine -c 'uname -a'
.fi
.TP
one ARM64 command with no retained container
.nf
wsl-toolkit run --image alpine --platform linux/arm64 --container-lifecycle ephemeral -c 'uname -m'
.fi
.TP
a script file rather than a string
.nf
wsl-toolkit run --image debian --script .\\build.sh
.fi
.TP
a workspace copied in and artifacts back
.nf
wsl-toolkit run --image debian --workspace . --artifacts .\\out -c 'make && cp build/x /out/'
.fi
.TP
the same command across every catalog image, with no retained containers
.nf
wsl-toolkit matrix --images all --container-lifecycle ephemeral -c 'cc --version'
.fi
.TP
no network for the container
.nf
wsl-toolkit run --image alpine --no-network -c 'wget -T2 example.com'
.fi
.TP
as an account that is not root
.nf
wsl-toolkit run --image alpine --user 1000:1000 -c 'id -u'
.fi
.TP
read a job's complete output back
.nf
wsl-toolkit logs JOB-ID
.fi
.TP
why a job failed, after the container is gone
.nf
wsl-toolkit inspect JOB-ID
.fi
.TP
inspect and remove one retained job
.nf
wsl-toolkit inspect JOB-ID ; wsl-toolkit gc --job JOB-ID --apply
.fi
.TP
two agents, isolated from each other
.nf
wsl-toolkit --instance two ready --ensure
.fi
.TP
what this tool is holding, and release it
.nf
wsl-toolkit resources ; wsl-toolkit gc --apply
.fi
.TP
a whole throwaway distribution, removed when its command ends
.nf
wsl-toolkit distro new --image alpine --ephemeral -c 'cat /etc/os-release'
.fi
.TP
keep one, run in it again, then remove it
.nf
wsl-toolkit distro new --image debian --name build-box ; wsl-toolkit distro run --name build-box -c 'uname -a' ; wsl-toolkit distro remove --name build-box --yes
.fi
.TP
a long command in one, watched, recorded and compared with an earlier run
.nf
wsl-toolkit distro run --name build-box --log-profile ci --event-log .\\run.jsonl -c 'make' ; wsl-toolkit distro compare --before .\\earlier.jsonl --after .\\run.jsonl
.fi
.TP
the address a distribution reaches this host at
.nf
wsl-toolkit hostaddress
.fi
.TP
a caller that cannot reach wsl.exe
.nf
wsl-toolkit helper serve --detach
.fi
.TP
move to a newer release
.nf
wsl-toolkit selfupdate --check
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
Run \fBwsl-toolkit examples\fR for executable examples and \fBwsl-toolkit COMMAND --help\fR for direct help.
